Fetched at pinned commits during builds, never vendored:
- lky005/ruby-ios-bringup: MIT for its code and documentation; its XNU patches
  are APSL-2.0. Its ci/ scripts are run unmodified from the pinned commit.
- MakrSas/ios-topaz: XNU patch baseline (sweet 0001-0079 lineage, from
  lgrachov/ios-qemu and its predecessors). The repository declares no licence;
  its patches modify Apple XNU (APSL-2.0) and ios-qemu's tools are MIT.
- blacktop/darwin-xnu-build: MIT.
- Apple XNU and other Apple open source: APSL-2.0 and per-file licences.

CI artifacts contain only a kernel built from those open sources with Apple's
toolchain; no SDK headers, KDK, firmware or iOS material is published.
The iOS userland and any Apple software come from the user's own copies under
Apple's licence and are never distributed by this project.

